# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# The move at the section's end, its stutters, from F#3 (the lowest black key, key 1), on any screen: each press the
# next move (STUTTER SIMPLE, STUTTER COMPLEX, DRUM FILL, COMP FILL, OFF), said; F#3 blinks while one waits (the shared
# 250 ms blink: key_blink, bit 1), dark once it has played. A stutter plays on the last bar of the section playing, in
# place of the song's own there; queued past its figure's catch there, the next section's. The first song is 56 bars at
# 81 BPM (2963 ms a bar, a 16th 185 ms): an 8-bar intro (bar 8, from 0: 7, about 22.2-25.2 s), four 8-bar grooves (no
# lead), two lead blocks.
listen
wait 1400
tap PLAY
wait 3000
expect move 0
expect key_blink 0
# F#3 through all five, each said; the stutters and fills wait for the intro's last bar
tapkey 1
said END STUTTER SIMPLE
expect move 3
expect move_at 7
expect key_blink 2
expect hold -1
tapkey 1
said END STUTTER COMPLEX
expect move 4
tapkey 1
said END DRUM FILL
expect move 1
tapkey 1
said END COMP FILL
expect move 2
tapkey 1
said END OFF
expect move 0
expect move_at -1
expect key_blink 0
# on Sections too: twice, a complex stutter
tap SEL
wait 50
said SECTIONS
tapkey 1
tapkey 1
wait 50
said END STUTTER COMPLEX
expect move 4
expect move_at 7
expect key_blink 2
shot stutter-queued.png
# the intro's last bar, early (about 22.6 s): it landed there, a complex figure, still shown (it hasn't caught yet)
wait 17310
expect bar 7
expect stutter_bar 7
expect stutter_fig >2
expect move 4
expect key_blink 2
# its replays (the bar's 16th, about 25.0 s): the mix stutters, K3 back to OFF, F#3 dark
wait 2250
expect bar 7
expect stuttering 1
expect move 0
expect key_blink 0
wait 1000
expect bar 8
expect stutter_bar -1
shot stutter-played.png
# the first groove's last bar (bar 16, from 0: 15; 45.9-48.9 s), past a simple figure's catch (its 14th 16th, about
# 48.3 s): it rolls to the next section's last bar (bar 24, from 0: 23)
wait 22300
expect bar 15
tapkey 1
wait 50
said END STUTTER SIMPLE
expect bar 15
expect move 3
expect move_at 23
# bar 24, early (about 70.0 s): landed, a simple figure
wait 21560
expect bar 23
expect stutter_bar 23
expect stutter_fig <3
expect move 3
wait 2200
expect bar 23
expect stuttering 1
expect move 0
expect key_blink 0
# stopped, a press queues one all the same (F#3 blinks); PLAY: the song goes on from the bar it stopped in (bar 24, from
# 0: 23, its start), a section's last: the stutter lands there again, shown until it catches
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
tapkey 1
said END STUTTER SIMPLE
expect move 3
expect key_blink 2
tap PLAY
wait 1500
expect playing 1
expect move 3
expect bar 23
expect stutter_bar 23
expect move_at -1
# four more presses (COMPLEX, DRUM FILL, COMP FILL, OFF): cancelled
tapkey 1
tapkey 1
tapkey 1
tapkey 1
said END OFF
expect move 0
expect key_blink 0
